## Set up in this order

1. [Install the theme](install.html).
2. [Choose a theme colour](colour-settings.html).
3. Review [compatibility](compatibility.html) for native and third-party components.
4. Apply the [design styles](../styles/index.html) and [writing guide](../content/index.html).
5. Optionally [add a family name, crest or business logo](personalisation.html).
6. Use [components](../components/index.html) and [patterns](../patterns/index.html) for new work.
7. Run the [release checks](../accessibility/testing.html) before deploying a change.

## Design principles

- Show useful information before decorative content.
- Preserve Home Assistant's native navigation, keyboard behaviour and permissions.
- Make states and actions understandable without colour alone.
- Use one set of semantic tokens across all maintained components.
- Keep essential controls available at narrow widths and high zoom.
- Document deliberate deviations and the user need they serve.

Civica adapts the [GOV.UK Design System](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/) to repeated home use. More icons, continuous controls and live data are fine when they make a household task clearer.
